        "content": "<p>Firestar99 opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15115\">PR #15115</a> from <code>Firestar99:pulley_missing_feature</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>cargo b -p cranelift-codegen --no-default-features --features all-arch,std</code> fails to compile on main. Not sure how your CI setup works, and whether you want to add anything to check disabling features actually works.</p>\n<p>Going full <code>no_std</code> with <code>cargo b -p cranelift-codegen --no-default-features --features all-arch</code> still fails to compile due to s390x using <code>f32::powi()</code>, which is a <code>#[rustc_allow_incoherent_impl]</code> so even though it's declared in <code>core</code>, it only \"exists\" in <code>std</code>. Could be fixed by depending on <code>num-traits</code> and <code>libm</code>, which will provide a software impl in <code>no_std</code> scenarios, but probably noone cares enough about <code>no_std</code> for this to really matter. Also shoutout to <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/137578\"><code>core_float_math</code> rustc feature</a> which should fix this.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636890410,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793627208
    },
